WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.315
"Diverticulosis Diet: Should Nuts, Seeds,
and Popcorn Be Avoided?"

00:00:06.859 --> 00:00:10.760
Diverticulosis involves
abnormal outpouchings

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.800
from the wall of our colon,
affecting most people

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.440
by the time
they reach their 60s

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.040
whether they know it or not.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.800
In as many as 10 to 25 percent
of individuals

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.880
these outpouchings
can become inflamed

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.240
and turn the diverticulosis
into diverticulitis,

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.640
resulting in hundreds
of thousands of ER visits

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.600
and hospitalizations

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.880
and, sometimes, even leading
to perforation of the colon,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.200
which may have a fatality rate
as high as one in five.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.720
But it wasn't always like this.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.160
Diverticulosis only became
a problem in the 20th century.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.080
What is now a massive epidemic
didn't even start showing up

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.880
in medical textbooks
until 1920.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:52.800
Diverticulosis appeared
to be a deficiency disease

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.440
of Western civilization.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.840
Just like scurvy is
a deficiency disease

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.520
caused by a lack of vitamin C,

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.520
diverticulosis may be
a deficiency disease

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.680
caused by lack of fiber.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.560
Bowel movements
should be effortless,

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.640
but when we don't get enough
fiber-containing foods

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.520
in our diet,
like whole grains and beans,

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.560
we have to strain to push
unnaturally firm stools.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.080
The pressure necessary to force
along small, hard stools

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.320
may essentially blow pouches
out of the wall of our colon

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:27.040
like when you squeeze
one of those gel stress balls.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.640
As we got better and better
at refining grains

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.520
and stripping away the fiber,

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.000
diverticulosis rates
shot up to epidemic levels.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.560
What about populations
like those in rural Africa

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.720
where they were eating up
to the triple digit grams a day

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.680
that we, as a species,
were meant to get

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.880
based on Paleolithic
diet estimates

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.000
and paleopoo fossilized feces?

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.760
Diverticulosis remained
almost completely absent

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.400
in areas that continued
to center their diets

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.840
around whole plant foods,

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.640
the only foods where fiber
is found in abundance.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.800
So, just like heart disease
is the number one killer

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.600
in the United States

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.600
and was virtually unknown
in rural Africa,

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.560
diverticulosis was
also virtually unknown;

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.320
whereas it's the most common
disease of the colon here

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.920
and around
the Westernized world.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.360
Migration studies prove

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.920
it's not some genetic
racial difference either.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.480
The prevalence
of diverticulosis

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.160
was one percent in Japan.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.360
At the same time,
it was 50 times higher

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.160
in Japanese people
who started eating

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.440
and living like Americans.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.360
Higher fiber intake
may also explain why vegetarians

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.480
may be up to nearly three times
less likely

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.240
to be affected
by this condition.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.040
Today, increasing fiber intake
is accepted

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:42.640
as the overriding
dietary recommendation

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.280
for people afflicted
with diverticulosis,

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.720
but what about
the common advice from doctors

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.480
telling patients
with the condition

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.120
not to eat nuts, seeds,
and corn?

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.040
The rationale was that
these foods could get lodged

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.040
in one
of the outpouching pockets

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.080
and trigger inflammation,

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.200
but the myth that we should
avoid eating nuts, corn,

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.280
popcorn, and seeds to prevent
episodes like diverticulitis

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.280
has been debunked
with modern data.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.440
In fact, Harvard researchers
looked into this

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.920
and actually found
protective associations

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.832
between nut
and popcorn consumption

00:03:15.832 --> 00:03:17.560
and the risk of diverticulitis.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.080
So, doctors should be telling
patients with diverticulosis

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.000
that they can eat nuts, corn,
and popcorn without fear,

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.440
advice echoed by Harvard,

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.560
by the Mayo Clinic,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.120
and the Cleveland Clinic,

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.000
where the avoidance advice
was identified

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.960
as the number one myth.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.840
A healthy, high-fiber diet
is actually the best medicine

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.160
against diverticulitis,

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.640
and nuts and seeds
certainly fit the bill.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.720
In fact, increasing
dietary fiber intake

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.040
should be seen
as a major public health issue

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.120
that may have
a dramatic beneficial effect

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.760
in diet-related diseases
and deaths, in general.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:53.584
In other words,
eat more plants.

